## Findings (ranked)
F1 HIGH — tag-collision stranding. packages/mpd-worktree-plugin/src/git.ts -> checkedOutBranch uses 'git rev-parse --abbrev-ref HEAD'; a branch named like an existing tag abbreviates to 'heads/<name>' and revalidateRecordedBranch refuses branch-mismatch forever. Evidence: probe-ambiguity.log (feature tag; agent/alice tag), probe-head-tag.log (HEAD source removes fine -> regression introduced by the uncommitted change), probe-branch-plumbing.log (branch --show-current = feature vs abbrev-ref = heads/feature), probe-ambiguity-recovery.log (manual rm needed).
F2 MEDIUM — full-ref spelling bypass. packages/mpd-worktree-plugin/src/ops.ts -> createEntry protected check is exact-string; branch 'refs/heads/dev' (with dev existing and protected) creates, then remove/merge refuse branch-mismatch; emptying protectedBranches does not help. Evidence: probe-refspelling.log. Fix at creation: reject refs/-rooted names (or canonicalise with a round-trip proof).
F3 NIT — docs guarantee is stronger than the code for the spellings above; becomes true once F1/F2 are fixed, otherwise qualify.

