## Declined to judge
- Pre-existing records already on a now-protected branch: no migration added; recovery is a config change named by the create refusal; outside the frozen creation scope.
- A later config change adding protection deliberately freezes remove/merge; operator-owned and force-blind by design.
- protectedBranches entries are not trimmed; pre-existing config behaviour untouched by this diff.
- Linux-only; case-insensitive filesystems/Windows not exercised.
- Non-tag ref ambiguity not exhaustively enumerated; the tag case is proven and the symbolic-ref fix covers the class.
- Refusal precedence (protected vs name/path/cap) not part of the frozen ordering; all paths side-effect free.
- Reattach refusal leaves the record active while protected; intended degrade, recovery works once unprotected (probe D9/D10).
- Merge target force:true still bypasses target protection; unchanged and documented.
- Pre-N1 wrong-ref merge semantics for full-ref spellings are masked here by branch-mismatch; not separately audited.

## Bounds
- No live harness boot or real mounted tool call; the tool surface was captured through a minimal adapter/ctx double and the registered execute was invoked. Dist verified byte-identical to a pinned rebuild, not executed.
- No Docker lane, no full-repo bun test, no network.
- Falsifiability re-proven on a git-archive HEAD copy (scratch removed), never by editing the working tree.
- Read: worktree plugin src/test/dist surface, four docs, relevant .mpd/plans/agent-worktrees.md sections. Not read: unrelated packages, whole plan, full upstream contract.
- The F4 creation guard itself is verified; F1/F2 are in the same uncommitted N1 change (checkedOutBranch / revalidateRecordedBranch).

